Proceed immediately to the Emergency Department if you develop sudden shortness of breath, severe chest pain, painful swelling strictly in one leg, or a high fever, as you are at high risk for blood clots and severe infections.

PATIENT INFORMATION

Disclaimer: This condition represents a severe structural leak in the kidney filters requiring specialist management and likely a kidney biopsy.
Clinical Course: The kidney filters are damaged, allowing massive amounts of protein to spill into the urine. Without protein in the blood to hold fluid in the vessels, water rapidly leaks into the face and tissues. Specialized medications like steroids are required to stop the leak.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Do not attempt to take over-the-counter water pills (diuretics) without specialist instruction. Because fluid has leaked out of your blood vessels into your tissues, your actual blood volume is dangerously low; taking water pills now could cause sudden kidney failure.

